  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table><thead><tr><th><div>Sputum Culture Result</div></th><th><div>Interpretation</div></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><div>No Significant Growth</div></td><td><div>No significant growth of pathogenic microorganisms is observed in the sputum culture. This indicates that there are no detectable pathogens causing respiratory infection.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Positive Result (with Identifiable Pathogens)</div></td><td><div>A positive result with identifiable pathogens indicates the presence of specific microorganisms in the sputum culture. The report may specify the type of bacteria, fungi, or other microorganisms isolated from the sample. The sensitivity testing will also determine which antibiotics or antifungal medications are effective against the identified pathogens.</div></td></tr><tr><td><div>Contaminated Result</div></td><td><div>In some cases, the sputum culture may show the growth of non-pathogenic bacteria or contaminants from the upper respiratory tract or environment. This is considered a contaminated result and may not be indicative of an actual respiratory infection. Repeat testing may be necessary.</div></td></tr></tbody></table>",
